# SharePlate repository vulnerability risk acceptances
# Reviewed: 2026-07-29
# Owner: DevSecOps
# Reviewer: CI/CD team
#
# These exceptions apply only to the repository filesystem scan.
# They must not be passed to Docker image scans.
# Every acceptance expires on 2026-12-31 and must then be reviewed again.

# Direct dependency: react-router-dom -> react-router.
# SharePlate does not use the unstable React Server Components APIs required
# for this vulnerability to be exploitable. A major-version upgrade to the
# fixed release requires separate compatibility testing.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 exp:2026-12-31

# Transitive frontend build dependency: react-scripts -> SVGR/SVGO -> nth-check.
# Used during asset compilation; it is not shipped as an application API that
# processes attacker-controlled selector expressions at runtime.
CVE-2021-3803 exp:2026-12-31

# Transitive frontend build dependencies through react-scripts tooling.
# These packages process build inputs rather than untrusted production requests.
# Replacement requires migration away from the affected react-scripts toolchain.
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-27601 exp:2026-12-31
GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq exp:2026-12-31
GHSA-2p49-hgcm-8545 exp:2026-12-31

# Transitive PostCSS build dependency introduced by resolve-url-loader.
# SharePlate does not accept or process user-supplied CSS at runtime.
# Upgrade is pending compatibility testing of the frontend build toolchain.
CVE-2026-45623 exp:2026-12-31
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 exp:2026-12-31